    "Gap phases are disjoint clock accounting, not independent causes.",
    "Critical execution spans include CPU submission stalls and output joins.",
    "Snapshot precedes membership accounting; both timestamps are retained.",
    "Counterfactual deadlines hold future arrival/KV/ack traces fixed; changed membership would change that future.",
    "Observed readiness is the last logged snapshot, not instantaneous readiness.",
    "Candidate readiness after the actual seal is unobserved; hypothetical later timers report no readiness count.",
    "Changing prediction can change wakeups and future batches even when readiness exits first.",
    "No forecast or GPU execution is modified; this retrospective audit does not identify a causal throughput effect."
